1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:06,500
Anthropic 刚刚警告说，AI 改进 AI 的重大门槛可能近在咫尺。
Anthropic just warned us that it could be approaching a major threshold for AI improving AI.

2
00:00:06,720 --> 00:00:15,940
现在，一份来自 Meter Research 的独立报告让我们
看到了幕后的情况，包括尚未发布的模型测试结果。
And now, an independent report from Meter Research gives us a look at what's happening behind the scenes,
including results from clawed models that are unreleased.

3
00:00:16,430 --> 00:00:24,900
与此同时，OpenAI 发布了一个在网络安全领域评级为关键的新模型，
而且 AI 仍在帮助研究人员取得更多的科学发现。
Meanwhile, OpenAI has a new model rated critical in cybersecurity, and
AI is continuing to help researchers make more scientific discoveries.

4
00:00:25,360 --> 00:00:31,680
但在本周的美国大选之后，针对 AI 和数据中心的抵制情绪越来越难以忽视。
But after this week's US elections, the pushback against AI and data centers is getting harder to ignore.

5
00:00:31,918 --> 00:00:36,932
AI 股票正在遭受重创，而且要求放缓这一进程的呼声日益高涨。
AI stocks are getting hammered, and there's growing calls to slow this whole thing down.

6
00:00:37,280 --> 00:00:40,932
那么，AI 到底在多快的速度上加速？
So, how fast is AI actually accelerating?

7
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:44,400
政府又会采取多大的措施来放缓它？
And how far will governments go to slow it down?

8
00:00:44,686 --> 00:00:45,360
让我们切入正题。
Let's get into it.

9
00:00:45,614 --> 00:00:49,920
好了，Anthropic 本周更新了它的 IPO 申报文件。
Alright, so Anthropic just updated its IPO filing this week.

10
00:00:50,080 --> 00:00:57,892
在第 29 页，他们增加了一个关于 RSI，也就是递归自我改进的新段落。
And in it, over on page 29, they added this new paragraph about RSI, recursive self-improvement.

11
00:00:58,158 --> 00:01:09,480
他们写道：我们关于此类 AI 驱动加速速度的大部分证据源自滞后指标，
而且我们预测或衡量能力进步速度的能力有限，包括归因于我们最新或未发布模型的任何加速。
They wrote, Much of our evidence regarding the pace of such AI-driven acceleration is derived from lagging indicators,
and our ability to forecast or measure the rate at which our capabilities are advancing,

12
00:01:09,480 --> 00:01:14,660
他们写道：我们关于此类 AI 驱动加速速度的大部分证据源自滞后指标，
而且我们预测或衡量能力进步速度的能力有限，包括归因于我们最新或未发布模型的任何加速。
including any acceleration attributable to our most recent or unreleased models, is limited.

13
00:01:14,894 --> 00:01:26,436
因此，过去我们未能识别，未来也可能无法识别出研发速度的显著加速，直到它已经发生之后。
As a result, we have in the past not identified, and may in the future not identify,
a significant acceleration in our rate of development until after it has occurred.

14
00:01:26,702 --> 00:01:41,444
例如，我们的内部评估和对未来模型的预期（而非当前模型）表明，
我们可能即将达到负责任扩展政策中关于 AI 驱动的剧烈加速进步的定义。
For example, our internal estimates and our expectations regarding future models rather than our current models indicate that we may
imminently meet a responsible scaling policy's definition of dramatically accelerated progress attributable to AI.

15
00:01:41,760 --> 00:01:49,508
所以基本上，他们是在说 AI 正在帮助他们构建更好的 AI，
而且速度快到足以触发他们自己的安全阈值。
So basically, they're talking about AI helping them build better AI here, fast enough to trigger one of their own safety thresholds.

16
00:01:49,838 --> 00:01:58,916
他们还没有宣布任何当前或未发布的模型已经跨越了这一阈值，但他们也警告说，
他们可能只有在跨越之后才能意识到它已经被跨越了。
They haven't declared that any current or unreleased models have crossed it, but they
also warn that they might only recognize it's been crossed after it's been crossed.

17
00:01:59,278 --> 00:02:00,932
这可能会迫使他们放慢速度。
This could then force them to slow down.

18
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:06,960
这就引出了那份新的 Meter 报告，它让我们更清楚地看到实际发生了什么。
And that brings us to the new meter report that gives us a better look at what's actually going on.

19
00:02:07,246 --> 00:02:14,560
研究小组 Meter 对 Anthropic 在 10 月份的 AI 研发加速进行了独立的评估。
So the research group meter has done their own independent assessment of anthropics AI RD acceleration in the month of October.

20
00:02:14,720 --> 00:02:24,080
他们发现，自去年 10 月 2025 年以来，基准测试的进步速度大约快了 1.9 倍。
And what they've found is that benchmark progress has been roughly 1.9 times faster since last year in October 2025.

21
00:02:24,398 --> 00:02:28,480
想想看，大约两年的进步在一年内就完成了。
Think roughly two years of progress at the old pace happening in one year.

22
00:02:28,654 --> 00:02:31,200
根据他们的说法，这就是现在的改进速度。
That's about the rate of improvement now, according to them.

23
00:02:31,470 --> 00:02:43,300
他们实际上说，这些新的内部模型——也就是我们稍后要重点讨论的橙色标注模型——让永久性的斜
率变化看起来比 Mythos 预览中的一次性跳跃更具可能性。
They actually say these new internal models, the ones highlighted in orange that we're going to talk more about shortly,
make a permanent slope change look more plausible than a one-time jump at Mythos preview.

24
00:02:43,520 --> 00:02:47,840
这意味着，这种新的增长速度现在可能就是常态。
Meaning essentially this new rate of growth might just be the norm now.

25
00:02:48,046 --> 00:02:49,412
而这里就是有趣的地方。
And here's where it gets interesting.

26
00:02:49,680 --> 00:03:02,480
同样，这包括我们无法获取的内部模型，比如 8 月和 9 月完成训练的 Model 3，
甚至包括 9 月和 10 月完成的 Model 4。
Again, this is including internal models we haven't had access to, such as Model 3, which finished training in August, September,
and even Model 4, which finished in September, October.

27
00:03:02,702 --> 00:03:11,080
我记得 Anthropic 在最近的一篇帖子中含糊地提到了 Model 2，
但我猜现在我们已经进入 Model 3 和 Model 4 了，当然，这些是他们下一代模型的占位名称。
I remember when Anthropic vaguely talked about Model 2 in one of their recent posts,
but I guess now we've already moved on to Model 3 and Model 4, these,

28
00:03:11,080 --> 00:03:15,044
我记得 Anthropic 在最近的一篇帖子中含糊地提到了 Model 2，
但我猜现在我们已经进入 Model 3 和 Model 4 了，当然，这些是他们下一代模型的占位名称。
of course, being placeholder names for their next generation models.

29
00:03:15,310 --> 00:03:21,700
他们实际上在报告中没有提供太多关于 Model 3 的
细节，你可以想象这是他们即将发布的下一个模型。
They actually don't give us much detail about Model 3 in this report, which you can imagine is their next model being released.

30
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:31,108
但这里他们专门用了一个章节讲 Model 4，显然它在用
于能力指数的所有 15 项基准测试中得分都超过了 50%。
But here they have a whole section on Model 4, which apparently scored above 50% on all 15 benchmarks used for its capability index.

31
00:03:31,374 --> 00:03:39,120
你可以从这里的图表中看到，虽然有点乱，但 Model 4 在最右边，
每一条深色线条代表一个不同的基准测试。
You can see here in the graph, it's a little bit messy, but model four is on the far right,
and each of these darker colored lines represents a different benchmark.

32
00:03:39,310 --> 00:03:42,880
看看这些线条在仅仅 9 个月前的 Opus 4.6 时的位置。
Look at where those lines were for Opus 4.6, just nine months earlier.

33
00:03:43,040 --> 00:03:44,720
还有一大部分都低于 50%。
A bunch were still below 50%.

34
00:03:45,280 --> 00:03:51,844
但现在，这 15 项测试全部都超过了这个比例，我认为这是首次出现这种情况。
Now though, every one of these 15 tests is above it, which I think is the first time this has ever happened.

35
00:03:52,110 --> 00:03:55,840
员工还报告说，使用它后的生产力提高了大约 12 倍。
Employees also reported roughly 12 times the productivity with it.

36
00:03:56,238 --> 00:03:56,900
12 倍。
12 times.

37
00:03:57,230 --> 00:03:57,892
这简直太疯狂了。
That is insane.

38
00:03:58,158 --> 00:04:05,668
你可以看到这个内部指标已经在飙升了，但现在它似乎以某种方式，
甚至可能是指数级地更猛烈地飙升。
You can see this internal metric has already been skyrocketing, but now it's skyrocketing even more, somehow, seemingly exponentially.

39
00:04:05,998 --> 00:04:09,828
所以你可能在想，到底是什么造成了这一切？
So you're probably wondering, what's actually causing all this?

40
00:04:10,256 --> 00:04:18,736
嗯，不出所料，METR 初步将目前约 80% 的加速直接归功于 AI。
Well, unsurprisingly, meter tentatively attributes about 80% of the current acceleration directly to AI.

41
00:04:18,926 --> 00:04:34,468
事实上，他们甚至暗示 2025 年底的加速可能受到非 AI 因素的影响，但现在的加速，
也就是 2026 年 10 月，肯定主要是与 AI 相关的，我觉得这一点挺有意思的。
In fact, they even suggest the acceleration in late 2025 was likely influenced by non-AI factors, but that the acceleration now,
in October 2026, is again definitely mostly AI related, which I thought was pretty interesting.

42
00:04:34,896 --> 00:04:38,656
那么，这是否意味着递归自我改进已经实现了？
Now, does this mean recursive self-improvement is here?

43
00:04:38,896 --> 00:04:46,496
我的意思是，就基于我们今年年底看到的一切，我个人会说是的，至少是它的开端。
I mean, personally, I'd say yes, at least the beginnings of it, just
based off of everything we've been seeing towards the end of this year.

44
00:04:46,576 --> 00:04:47,492
现在又有了这个。
And now this.

45
00:04:47,822 --> 00:04:59,204
但如果你问 Anthropic，他们的政策实际上允许在 AI 开发大幅加速时发出警告，
甚至在模型能够取代其整个研究团队之前。
But if you ask Anthropic, their policy actually allows for a warning threshold based on dramatically accelerated AI development,
even before models can replace its entire research staff.

46
00:04:59,534 --> 00:05:11,332
所以显然，在 AI 开始让构建更好 AI 的过程变得快得多的同时，人类仍能参与其中，
这几乎就是现在正在发生的事情，这也是他们更新 IPO 文件的原因。
So humans can still be involved while AI starts making the process of building better AI much faster, obviously,
which is pretty much exactly what's happening now, hence the updates to their IPO filing.

47
00:05:11,566 --> 00:05:19,616
当然，在训练过程中仍有一些关键阶段，模型还没有做出重大贡献，人类仍然深度参与其中。
There's still, of course, crucial stages of training where the models aren't
making major contributions autonomously, that humans are still very much a part of.

48
00:05:19,886 --> 00:05:27,172
但 METR 也表示，他们尚未确定一个令人信服的基准，能在未来一年内阻止这种加速。
But Meter also says they haven't really identified a convincing benchmark yet that would stop this acceleration over the next year.

49
00:05:27,536 --> 00:05:28,416
所以，是的。
So yeah.

50
00:05:28,750 --> 00:05:31,536
简单来说，他们预计这种情况会持续下去。
To put it simply, they expect this to continue.

51
00:05:31,696 --> 00:05:35,456
而且记住，我们看到的只是冰山一角。
And remember, we're only seeing part of the picture anyways.

52
00:05:35,758 --> 00:05:42,736
Anthropic 显然删减了这项评估中一些最有信息量的证据，包括涉及未来模型的预测。
Anthropic apparently redacted some of the most informative evidence behind this assessment,
including a forecast involving a future model.

53
00:05:42,926 --> 00:05:47,428
也就是说，有一些信息支撑了这些结论，但我们目前还看不到。
So there's information feeding into these conclusions that we just don't get to see yet.

54
00:05:47,758 --> 00:05:50,256
这就回到了 S1 文件中的那个警告。
Which brings us back to that warning in the S1.

55
00:05:50,478 --> 00:05:55,812
Anthropic 表示，他们可能只有在显著加速发生后才能察觉到。
Anthropic said it might only recognize a significant acceleration after it's already happened.

56
00:05:56,046 --> 00:05:56,896
这就是关键点。
That's the key thing.

57
00:05:57,198 --> 00:06:04,580
所以，如果模型在帮助构建下一代模型并使其不断变强，
在我们意识到发生了什么之前，这速度会快到什么程度？
So if the model is helping build the next generation keep getting better,
how much faster does this get before we even realize what's happening?

58
00:06:04,896 --> 00:06:08,164
或者在 Anthropic 意识到发生了什么之前。
Or before Anthropic even realizes what's happening.

59
00:06:08,430 --> 00:06:17,776
我的意思是，我们之所以能知道这些尚未发布的内部模型，
也就是模型 3 和模型 4，完全是因为 METR 的研究。
I mean, the only reason we're even finding out about this, about these unreleased
internal models, model three and model four, is because of meter research.

60
00:06:17,936 --> 00:06:20,900
我相信这是它们第一次被公开提及。
I believe this is the first time they've ever even been publicly mentioned.

61
00:06:21,216 --> 00:06:30,096
现在说到 AI 改进 AI，本周还有另一个实验，其中一个
AI 实际上修改了另一个 AI 的模型权重来让它变得更好。
Now, speaking of AI improving AI, there was another experiment this week
where an AI actually edited another AI's model weights to make it better.

62
00:06:30,318 --> 00:06:34,660
我昨天已经做了一个完整的视频来讲解这个，但让我快速给你们展示一下发生了什么。
I already made a full video on this yesterday, but let me quickly show you what happened.

63
00:06:34,976 --> 00:06:46,084
所以基本上，麻省理工学院的研究人员让 GBT6 Astra 访问了一个小型 Quen 模型，
并要求它在不运行常规训练过程的情况下提高模型的数学能力。
So basically, researchers at MIT gave GBT6 Astra access to a small Quen model
and asked it to make it better at math without running a normal training process.

64
00:06:46,382 --> 00:06:51,460
然后 Astra 发现了一个导致模型陷入推理循环的问题。
And Astra found an issue that was causing the model to get stuck in reasoning loops.

65
00:06:51,696 --> 00:07:04,548
接着它只修改了 0.016% 的权重，在相同的采样设置下，
该模型在数学基准测试中的得分从 7.9% 跃升到了 48.1%。
It then edited just 0.016% of the weights, and the model score on a math
benchmark jumped from 7.9% to 48.1% using the same sampling settings.

66
00:07:04,942 --> 00:07:12,548
也就是说，它只改变了模型内部极小比例的数值或权重，就大幅提升了它的表现。
So it changed just a tiny fraction of the actual numbers or weights inside the model and substantially improved how it performed.

67
00:07:12,782 --> 00:07:15,296
这在以前是大语言模型无法做到的事情。
This is not something LLMs were able to do before.

68
00:07:15,470 --> 00:07:17,776
而且其他人已经一直在尝试类似的事情。
And other people have already been trying similar things.

69
00:07:18,158 --> 00:07:29,260
例如，Lagora 的首席技术官说，他让 Fable 编写了一个小型神经网络的权重，
用于区分真实的法律引用和虚假的引用，基本上是直接创建了一个可用的网络，据他说，
Lagora's CTO, for example, says he got Fable to write the weights for a small neural network that distinguishes real from fake legal
citations, basically creating a working network directly, which he says initially beat his trained version.

70
00:07:29,260 --> 00:07:31,716
这最初甚至超过了他训练出的版本。
Lagora's CTO, for example, says he got Fable to write the weights for a small neural network that distinguishes real from fake legal
citations, basically creating a working network directly, which he says initially beat his trained version.

71
00:07:31,936 --> 00:07:36,260
所以这些实验还有很多细节，如果你错过了，我会把完整的解析链接发出来。
So there's a lot more to these experiments, and I'll link my full breakdown if you missed it.

72
00:07:36,496 --> 00:07:41,536
但是没错，这是 AI 构建和改进 AI 的另一种方法。
But yeah, this is another approach to AI building and improving AI.

73
00:07:41,678 --> 00:07:46,416
由此延伸开来，这也是我肯定会密切关注的 AI 理解领域。
And by extension, understanding AI that I'm definitely keeping an eye on.

74
00:07:46,880 --> 00:07:56,068
现在回到我们还没权限获取的模型话题，OpenAI 本周也悄悄向我们展示了一个新的内部模型。
Now, going back to the topic of models we don't have access to yet,
OpenAI also quietly showed us a new internal model of their own this week.

75
00:07:56,334 --> 00:07:59,556
这是在一篇关于使用 AI 进行物理工程的帖子中出现的。
This was in a post about using AI for physical engineering.

76
00:07:59,822 --> 00:08:09,156
就在下面，他们将它与 GBT6 Astra 在 BenchCAD 2.0 上的表现进行了对比，
该测试包含重建 3D 部件和推断电路板连接等内容。
And down here, they compare it with GBT6 Astra on BenchCAD 2.0, which tests things
like reconstructing 3D parts and figuring out connections in circuit boards.

77
00:08:09,454 --> 00:08:14,480
如你所见，Astra 在最高推理设置下的得分是 0.594。
As you can see, Astra at its highest reasoning setting scores 0.594.

78
00:08:14,720 --> 00:08:18,240
然而，这个更新的模型得分是 0.875。
This newer model, though, scores 0.875.

79
00:08:18,670 --> 00:08:20,160
这是一个相当大幅度的飞跃。
That's a pretty substantial jump.

80
00:08:20,320 --> 00:08:23,760
他们在这里没有给模型命名，但我们可以推测它可能是什么。
They don't name the model here, but we can speculate on what it might be.

81
00:08:23,950 --> 00:08:28,720
我猜这就是 GBT Aeon，最近我们经常听到它的消息。
I'm guessing this is GBT Aeon, which we've been hearing quite a bit about recently.

82
00:08:28,942 --> 00:08:32,558
在同一篇帖子中，他们展示了他们已经在使用 Astra 进行设计。
In this same post, they show that they've already been using Astra for design.

83
00:08:32,878 --> 00:08:38,788
两名员工实际上利用它在不到一周的时间内设计出了这个
与 Codex 对话的小装置，这只是他们的一个业余项目。
Two employees actually designed this little device for talking to Codex in under a week with it, as just a side project.

84
00:08:38,990 --> 00:08:42,080
该模型负责外壳、电路板和软件。
The model handled the enclosure, circuit board, and software.

85
00:08:42,381 --> 00:08:49,636
虽然为了准备生产仍需审查和迭代，但制造商在不
到一个月的时间内就生产出了原型，这速度非常快。
Getting it ready for manufacturing still took review and iteration, but a
manufacturer produced prototypes in under a month, which is pretty fast.

86
00:08:49,998 --> 00:09:01,760
所以我们已经看到 AI 帮助将创意转化为真实的实物，而 OpenAI
的下一个内部模型在执行这一任务上的得分已经明显更高了。
So we're already seeing AI help turn an idea into an actual physical object, while the next internal model OpenAI has is already
scoring considerably higher on doing exactly that.

87
00:09:02,062 --> 00:09:06,948
你可以想象，这对 OpenAI 来说是个好消息，尤其是考虑到他们即将推出的硬件设备。
You can imagine this is great news for OpenAI, especially with their upcoming hardware device.

88
00:09:07,374 --> 00:09:15,760
此外，OpenAI 本周还发布了另一项内容，让我们直接回到安全领域：GBT 6 cyber。
Now, OpenAI also released something else this week that takes us straight back to the security side of all this: GBT 6 cyber.

89
00:09:15,982 --> 00:09:24,228
在他们的准备框架下，他们将其在网络安全方面的级别划分为「关键」，
而 GBT 5.6 cyber 则是「高」。
They classify it as critical in cybersecurity under their preparedness framework, up from high for GBT 5.6 cyber.

90
00:09:24,462 --> 00:09:33,200
这是专门为网络安全工作训练的 Astra 版本，用于寻找漏洞、开发可用的漏洞利用程序，
并在获得授权的情况下测试系统。
This is a version of Astra specifically trained for cybersecurity work, finding
vulnerabilities, developing working exploits, and testing systems with permission.

91
00:09:33,390 --> 00:09:36,960
而且 Astra 显然也已经拥有了那个「关键」级别的评级。
And Astra apparently already had that critical designation too.

92
00:09:37,230 --> 00:09:40,800
Cyber 只是把这些能力进一步专业化。
Cyber just takes those capabilities and specializes them further.

93
00:09:41,006 --> 00:09:51,920
例如在 Exploit Gym 上，模型必须利用指定的漏洞，它的得分是 48.5%，
而之前的 cyber 模型是 32.1%。
